@Namespaces
.
=NAMESPACES
.
.NAMESPACE name ... END NAMESPACE groups names. Inside it a name is used
.bare. Outside it the name is qualified with a dot. ENDNAMESPACE is the same
.as END NAMESPACE.
.
:NAMESPACE GFX
:  DIM COLOR AS UBYTE
:  SUB PLOT(X AS UWORD, Y AS UBYTE)
:    POKE $9F20, COLOR
:  ENDSUB
:END NAMESPACE
:GFX.COLOR = 5
:GFX.PLOT(10, 20)
.
.  - A namespace body holds DIM, VAR, CONST, ENUM, SUB, FUNCTION, BIND,
.    ERRORS and other namespaces, and nothing that runs.
.  - A namespace may hold namespaces: OUTER.INNER.B is B in INNER in OUTER.
.  - A NAMESPACE with the name of one already made opens it again, to add
.    names.
.  - A name is found in the SUB or FUNCTION first, then in each namespace
.    around it, then in the main program. Inside OUTER, INNER.B and
.    OUTER.INNER.B are the same.
.  - A SUB's parameters and DIMs are local to it. Outside the SUB, SHOW.N
.    stops the compile with LOCAL TO A SUB: SHOW.N.
.  - UXC is a reserved name.
.
.See BIND, Types, Subroutines.
.
